msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandLine.md:221
msgid ""
"The CommandLine library uses a {ref}`different parser <different parser>` "
"for different data types. For example, in the string case, the argument "
"passed to the option is copied literally into the content of the string "
"variable... we obviously cannot do that in the boolean case, however, so we "
"must use a smarter parser.  In the case of the boolean parser, it allows no "
"options (in which case it assigns the value of true to the variable), or it "
"allows the values \"`true`\" or \"`false`\" to be specified, allowing any of "
"the following inputs:"
